 in closed session which required reporting. \r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\r The City Council approved the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS\r\rMayor Washburn presented a proclamation declaring March 2007 as �Safe Communities Month.� Mayor Washburn introduced Deputy Floyd Hayhurst, who spoke regarding the Association for Los Angeles Deputy Sheriffs (ALADS) and presented an award to the City of Calabasas for its support of public safety programs and the deputies who work in the City. Mayor pro Tem Bozajian congratulated staff on a successful Public Safety Appreciation Luncheon. He announced the upcoming Juan deAnza Days that will be taking place. Mayor pro Tem Bozajian spoke regarding the City Municipal Election and dates for the absentee ballot period. Councilmember Maurer spoke regarding a Girl Scout Troop mock City Council meeting that she hosted at City Hall. Mayor Washburn announced the upcoming MethodFest Film Festival.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r\rNidia Lota, Malibu, spoke regarding an experience she had with Councilmember Groveman. Sam Birenbaum, Los Angeles, spoke regarding Ms. Lota�s experience with Councilmember Groveman. David Shapiro, Calabasas, spoke regarding excessive noise in his neighborhood due to the Agoura Hills/Calabasas Community Center and The Cheesecake Factory facility.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS\r\r Approval of the minutes for the February 7, 2007 City Council meeting.\r \r Adoption of Ordinance No. 2007-233, adding Chapter 8.18 to the Calabasas Municipal Code regarding environmentally acceptable food packaging.\r\r Authorization for the City Manager to execute the fifth amendment to the Lease Agreement with Arden Realty, Inc., for City Hall, 26135 Mureau Road; and authorization to execute an amendment to the Lease Agreement with Kilroy Realty, for the Calabasas Library, 23975 Park Sorrento.\r\r Notice of completion for the stormscreen/stormchambers installation in private drain (P.D.) 1851, Project Specification No. 04-05-06.\r\r Recommendation to approve an amendment in the amount of $40,000 to the professional services agreement with Geodynamics for geotechnical services.\r\r Recommendation to extend the contract for an additional two years and increase the professional services agreement for plan check and geotechnical review with Wildan in the amount of $400,000.\r\rCouncilmember Maurer \u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, to approve Consent Items #1, 2, 3, 4, 5, and 6. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rSPECIAL PRESENTATION \r\r Report on success of School Area Traffic Safety Committee & the modification of public transit to serve school users.\r\rRobert Yalda, Public Works Director/City Engineer, presented the staff report.\r\rNo Action Taken.\r\rNEW BUSINESS\r\r Recommendation from the Library Commission for Civic Center Project Fundraising Consultant for a goal feasibility study. \r\rJohn Bingham, Senior Management Analyst, and Robin Parker, Assistant City Manager, presented the staff report.\r\rMayor pro Tem Bozajian moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to approve the Library Commission�s recommendation to contract with Netzel Associates, Inc. for a goal feasibility study for the Civic Center project fundraising. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r Discussion regarding contracting with a public mediator.\r\rThe City Council directed staff to invite the public mediation program to make a presentation to the City Council at a future meeting.\r\r\r\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS\r\r Check Register for the period of February 1, 2007 to February 8, 2007. \r\rNo action taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS\r\r Councilmember Maurer announced upcoming tours of Headwaters Corner. Councilmember Wolfson reported about the ongoing construction of the Civic Center.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT\r\r City Manager Coroalles spoke regarding a landscaping project in the medians on Parkway Calabasas. \r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS\r\r Mayor pro Tem Bozajian spoke regarding the recent correspondence to the United States Postal Service regarding service issues. The following items were requested to be placed on a future agenda:\r\rAn update on the rental registry program. \rAn update on the mobile home subsidy program. \rDiscussion regarding a proposed Congestion Mitigation Fee and the Long-range Air Quality Plan.\r\rADJOURN\r\r The City Council adjourned at 9:05 p.m.\r\r\r\r______________________________\rGwen Peirce, CMC\rAssistant City Clerk\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 2 -\u0015\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 3 -\u0015\r02/21/07\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0006\u0000\u0000\u0001\b\u0000\u0000\u0015\b\u0000\u0000\u0016\b\u0000\u0000r\b\u0000\u0000}\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000\r \u0000\u0000\u0016 \u0000\u0000= \u0000\u0000> \u0000\u0000� \u0000\u0000� \u0000\u0000� \u0000\u0000� \u0000\u0000� \u0000\u0000� \u0000\u0000G\n\u0000\u0000H\n\u0000\u0000I\n\u0000\u0000]\n\u0000\u0000^\n\u0000\u0000����ʿ�ʨ�����y�y���iTCT\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000 \u0015h�{�\u0000\u0016h\u0005 �\u0000OJ\u0003\u0000QJ\u0003\u0000aJ\u0018\u0000mH \u0010sH \u0010\u0000)\u0003j\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0015h�{�\u0000\u0016h\u0005 �\u0000OJ\u0003\u0000QJ\u0003\u0000U\b\u0001aJ\u0018\u0000mH \u0010sH \u0010\u001f\u0016h\u0005 �\u00005\b�>*\u0001OJ\u0003\u0000QJ\u0003\u0000\\\b�^J\u0003\u0000aJ\u0018\u0000\u0012\u0016h�\u0004\u000b\u0000OJ\u0003\u0000QJ\u0003\u0000^J\u0003\u0000\u0000\u0018\u0015h�[�\u0000\u0016h\u0005 �\u0000OJ\u0003\u0000QJ\u0003\u0000^J\u0003\u0000\u0000\u001b\u0016h\u0005 �\u00005\b�>*\u0001OJ\u0003\u0000QJ\u0003\u0000\\\b�^J\u0003\u0000\u0012\u0016h\u0005 �\u0000OJ\u0003\u0000